It sounds like she met up with 
Otonashi-san and is having a lot of fun.

00:14:41.030 --> 00:14:45.090
<i>I need something to cheer Fuyutsuki-san up.</i>

00:14:45.090 --> 00:14:47.520
<i>Let's see... Let's see...</i>

00:14:47.520 --> 00:14:49.770
What movie did you see?

00:14:49.770 --> 00:14:51.580
It's called <i>Rice</i>.

00:14:51.580 --> 00:14:53.290
What kind of movie is that?!

00:14:53.290 --> 00:14:56.320
It's a grand CG spectacle 
depicting the full life cycle

00:14:56.320 --> 00:14:58.280
of an anthropomorphized grain of rice!

00:14:58.280 --> 00:15:01.190
The climax is the threshing scene!

00:15:01.190 --> 00:15:04.290
And you enjoy that?

00:15:04.560 --> 00:15:07.040
Why would you see a movie like that?

00:15:07.040 --> 00:15:10.280
It had a lot of buzz 
and good reviews online,

00:15:10.280 --> 00:15:12.100
so I thought I'd try it out.

00:15:12.100 --> 00:15:13.080
For me...

00:15:13.550 --> 00:15:16.560
It's because you said you 
liked rice, Otonashi-san.

00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:19.430
Well, I like to <i>eat</i> rice...

00:15:19.430 --> 00:15:21.520
I'm not really interested 
in the threshing part.

00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:23.670
That reminds me.

00:15:23.670 --> 00:15:27.570
I saw Himuro-san and Fuyutsuki-san 
at the theater together!

00:15:27.570 --> 00:15:29.380
Hey, are you kidding me?!

00:15:29.380 --> 00:15:31.560
They went on a date to the movies?

00:15:32.020 --> 00:15:32.880
Yeah.

00:15:32.880 --> 00:15:34.710
What movie did they see?

00:15:35.180 --> 00:15:38.320
It wasn't <i>Rice</i>, I know that much.

00:15:38.320 --> 00:15:39.830
<i>Something...</i>

00:15:40.110 --> 00:15:42.800
<i>Something to cheer up Fuyutsuki-san...</i>

00:15:42.800 --> 00:15:45.330
<i>Something to cheer up Fuyutsuki-san...</i>

00:15:45.330 --> 00:15:48.340
Himuro-kun, would you like to play shiritori?

00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:50.760
The word chain game?

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:53.860
Is that childish?

00:15:53.860 --> 00:15:55.520
I'm sorry.

00:15:55.520 --> 00:15:58.350
I couldn't think of anything better to do.

00:15:58.840 --> 00:16:00.380
<i>Word chain...</i>

00:16:00.380 --> 00:16:03.840
<i>Does Fuyutsuki-san consider that fun?</i>

00:16:03.840 --> 00:16:06.850
<i>That's so freakin' cute!</i>

00:16:06.850 --> 00:16:09.670
No, it's an excellent idea.

00:16:09.670 --> 00:16:10.760
Let's try it.

00:16:11.360 --> 00:16:13.900
Okay, start with the "ri" in shiritori.

00:16:13.900 --> 00:16:14.720
Risu (squirrel).

00:16:14.720 --> 00:16:15.760
Surume (squid).

00:16:15.760 --> 00:16:16.500
Mesu (scalpel).

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:17.560
Suika (watermelon).

00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:18.870
Kakesu (jaybird).

00:16:19.320 --> 00:16:23.120
<i>Crud, I keep givin' her words that end with -su!</i>

00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:24.930
<i>What'll I do?</i>

00:16:24.930 --> 00:16:27.730
<i>I kinda feel like I'm bullyin' her...</i>

00:16:29.560 --> 00:16:31.280
<i>I knew it.</i>

00:16:31.730 --> 00:16:33.550
Su... su...

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:35.960
Uh, I-I'm not...

00:16:35.960 --> 00:16:38.380
<i>It ain't like that! It ain't!</i>

00:16:41.210 --> 00:16:42.640
Suki (love)...

00:16:46.040 --> 00:16:47.200
...yaki.

00:16:47.200 --> 00:16:48.760
<i>Sukiyaki?</i>

00:16:49.390 --> 00:16:51.400
<i>That scared me...</i>

00:16:51.780 --> 00:16:53.900
That day, they were showing...

00:16:53.900 --> 00:16:58.440
<i>George the Kitten</i>, <i>Rice</i>, 
<i>Attack of the Killer Fried Shrimp</i>,

00:16:58.440 --> 00:17:02.410
<i>A Love as Tenuous as Flower 
Petals</i>, <i>Tsundora Express</i>...

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:06.070
<i>George</i> is a family movie, 
so it's probably not that.

00:17:06.070 --> 00:17:12.430
I think a romance would freak Himuro-san 
out and throw the theater into chaos.

00:17:12.790 --> 00:17:14.660
The horror movie, then?

00:17:14.660 --> 00:17:19.930
I can't picture them getting 
scared and being all like, "Eek!"

00:17:21.180 --> 00:17:22.040
Kinoko (mushroom).

00:17:22.040 --> 00:17:22.920
Koara (koala).

00:17:22.920 --> 00:17:24.080
Rakko (sea otter).

00:17:24.080 --> 00:17:24.880
Konbu (seaweed).

00:17:24.880 --> 00:17:26.210
Buririanto katto (brilliant cut diamond).

00:17:26.210 --> 00:17:29.470
What's <i>Tsundora Express</i> about?

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:33.630
A kotatsu salesman and 
a hot springs owner meet

00:17:33.630 --> 00:17:35.720
on a train running through frozen Siberia...

00:17:35.720 --> 00:17:37.210
That's quite a coincidence!

00:17:37.210 --> 00:17:39.080
I can't really explain it,

00:17:39.080 --> 00:17:42.950
but the brakes cut out, and the 
train's barreling out of control.

00:17:42.950 --> 00:17:45.330
They have to work together 
to get out of trouble!

00:17:45.330 --> 00:17:46.450
It's an action movie!

00:17:46.450 --> 00:17:48.860
I think it's about the kotatsu salesman

00:17:48.860 --> 00:17:53.960
and hot springs owner falling in love 
by overcoming danger together.

00:17:53.960 --> 00:17:56.540
Oh, I know how that works!

00:17:56.540 --> 00:17:58.840
It's called the suspension 
bridge effect, right?

00:17:58.840 --> 00:18:03.470
People fall in love after riding out 
a dangerous situation together!

00:18:03.470 --> 00:18:05.520
Suspension bridge effect?

00:18:06.010 --> 00:18:10.470
Speaking of riding out danger, 
you think they're still working overtime?

00:18:10.680 --> 00:18:12.040
Ohmigod!

00:18:12.040 --> 00:18:16.240
You think they'll fall in love by riding 
out the danger of overtime?!

00:18:16.240 --> 00:18:17.730
That's it!

00:18:18.730 --> 00:18:19.850
Torunedo (tornado).

00:18:19.850 --> 00:18:21.060
Donatsu (donuts).

00:18:21.060 --> 00:18:22.390
Tsuinteeru (pigtails).

00:18:22.390 --> 00:18:23.920
Rukusenburuku (Luxembourg).

00:18:23.920 --> 00:18:25.320
Kurimanju (chestnut sweet cake).

00:18:25.740 --> 00:18:27.080
Ushimitsudoki (dead of night).

00:18:26.060 --> 00:18:28.170
<i>This is so much fun!</i>

00:18:27.640 --> 00:18:28.970
Kiritanpo (mashed rice).

00:18:28.600 --> 00:18:31.500
<i>I wish I could play shiritori all day!</i>

00:18:28.970 --> 00:18:30.550
Poruchinotake (Boletus mushroom).

00:18:35.500 --> 00:18:36.950
Yes, Fuyutsuki speaking.

00:18:36.950 --> 00:18:38.480
<i>Her call came in!</i>

00:18:38.480 --> 00:18:39.270
Yes.

00:18:39.260 --> 00:18:43.270
<i>Which means Fuyutsuki-san'll 
be goin' home after this.</i>

00:18:40.400 --> 00:18:41.600
Yes.

00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:43.270
I understand.

00:18:43.820 --> 00:18:46.490
<i>Wish time could stand still 
a little while longer.</i>

00:18:46.490 --> 00:18:47.270
Goodbye.

00:18:49.160 --> 00:18:51.780
Himuro-kun, I...

00:18:52.710 --> 00:18:54.380
Are you leaving now?

00:18:54.380 --> 00:18:55.690
That's good.

00:18:55.690 --> 00:18:57.010
I hope you have a nice night.

00:18:57.010 --> 00:18:57.750
No...

00:18:58.530 --> 00:19:01.610
My overtime's been extended.

00:19:02.040 --> 00:19:03.940
Well...

00:19:05.030 --> 00:19:06.440
Chin up.

00:19:06.440 --> 00:19:07.390
I know.

00:19:10.200 --> 00:19:11.420
Himuro-kun?

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:17.800
Do you find yourself doodling on whatever's
 at hand when you're on the phone?

00:19:17.800 --> 00:19:18.930
I do.

00:19:19.400 --> 00:19:20.650
<i>So cute!</i>

00:19:21.300 --> 00:19:26.060
I have no artistic talent, 
though, so this is all I can draw.

00:19:26.400 --> 00:19:27.680
A pig?

00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:28.870
It's a cat.

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:31.440
What's that of yours?

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:33.060
<b></b>Checking

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:33.060
<b></b>Later

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:33.060
<b></b>Call back

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:33.060
<b></b>Wait a while longer

00:19:31.440 --> 00:19:32.520
A bear.

00:19:35.560 --> 00:19:38.340
Should we try quizzing each other now?

00:19:38.810 --> 00:19:40.460
I accept.

00:19:40.950 --> 00:19:42.570
<b></b>Fuyutsuki-san

00:19:43.040 --> 00:19:44.380
Fuyutsuki-san!

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:47.650
What's with this picture?

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:48.080
<b></b>Fuyutsuki-san

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:48.080
<b></b>I changed my icon.

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:49.000
What is it?

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:50.440
Is it about work?

00:19:50.440 --> 00:19:53.640
No, she sent me some kind of picture—

00:19:55.380 --> 00:19:56.720
Himuro?

00:19:56.720 --> 00:19:58.090
He's blowing up my phone...

00:19:58.590 --> 00:20:00.210
<i>Listen up, Katori!</i>

00:19:58.590 --> 00:20:05.000
<b>Himuro</b>

00:20:00.210 --> 00:20:03.240
<i>Do you know who drew this 
icon portrait for me?!</i>

00:20:03.240 --> 00:20:04.820
<i>It was Fuyutsuki-san!</i>

00:20:04.820 --> 00:20:07.600
<i>And do you know who drew 
this icon for Fuyutsuki-san?!</i>

00:20:07.600 --> 00:20:08.520
<i>Me!</i>

00:20:08.520 --> 00:20:12.040
<i>I traded portraits with Fuyutsuki-san!</i>

00:20:12.850 --> 00:20:14.330
<i>Himuro!</i>

00:20:14.330 --> 00:20:17.360
<i>You've always had a more 
fiery soul than you let on.</i>

00:20:17.360 --> 00:20:19.260
<i>But I'll say one thing...</i>

00:20:19.690 --> 00:20:20.860
C-O-N...

00:20:21.390 --> 00:20:23.090
Congrats, Himuro!

00:20:25.860 --> 00:20:28.880
Katori-san? "Congrats" for what?

00:20:28.880 --> 00:20:32.910
My best friend Himuro made great 
progress with Fuyutsuki-san!

00:20:32.910 --> 00:20:34.880
So I said congrats!

00:20:35.590 --> 00:20:38.010
Great progress between 
Fuyutsuki-san and Himuro-san?

00:20:38.010 --> 00:20:39.800
What kind of progress?

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:42.920
You think surviving the dangers of overtime

00:20:42.920 --> 00:20:45.130
together inspired the 
suspension bridge effect?!

00:20:45.880 --> 00:20:49.100
They haven't responded.

00:20:49.100 --> 00:20:50.510
Same here.

00:20:50.510 --> 00:20:56.050
A shame. I wanted to hear their 
opinion of our icon exchange.

00:20:59.230 --> 00:21:00.760
Yes, Fuyutsuki speaking.

00:21:06.420 --> 00:21:08.160
Yes, Himuro speaking.

00:21:08.820 --> 00:21:10.760
Yes, understood.

00:21:10.760 --> 00:21:12.040
Goodbye.

00:21:15.680 --> 00:21:18.110
You can go home now?

00:21:18.110 --> 00:21:19.630
It seems so.

00:21:20.010 --> 00:21:21.430
W-Well, then...

00:21:21.960 --> 00:21:24.890
Would you like to grab a late 
dinner on the way back?

00:21:29.720 --> 00:21:31.320
I'll have to grab my things.

00:21:31.320 --> 00:21:33.080
Meet me at the entrance.

00:21:41.980 --> 00:21:44.740
<i>Best! Day! Ever!</i>

00:21:48.210 --> 00:21:51.800
What's the progress?! Why congrats?!

00:21:49.000 --> 00:21:50.560
He's not picking up...

00:21:51.800 --> 00:21:52.870
An engagement?

00:21:53.750 --> 00:21:56.840
The suspension bridge effect is amazing!

00:21:54.580 --> 00:21:56.840
I really doubt it's that.

00:23:28.970 --> 00:23:31.970
<b>George the Kitten</b>

00:23:28.970 --> 00:23:31.970
<b>Guaranteed at 28 points!</b>

00:23:32.180 --> 00:23:34.780
Th-This is...
